What this software does
-----------------------
It implements a third-party USB accessory that speaks the Android Open
Accessory (AOA) path used when DJI Goggles 2 stream live video to a phone
running DJI Fly. The goal is to display that feed on HDMI from a Raspberry Pi
without a phone, the DJI Fly app, or a commercial closed-source decoder.

No DJI binaries are redistributed
--------------------------------
This repository intentionally does **not** ship:

- DJI Fly APKs or native libraries
- DJI firmware images
- Vendor phone firmware dumps
- Proprietary closed-source decoder binaries from third parties

Protocol behaviour was learned from observing traffic on hardware the authors
own, and from independently written analysis tools. Runtime code in
`poc/pi_endpoint/` is original work of this project.

